    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ff371ecc",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in traditional Jewish attire (black coat, fur hat) energetically dancing or gesturing in a room filled with other men in similar attire, seated around long tables covered with plastic. The text overlay reads 'when the bass drops just right,' implying a humorous or exaggerated reaction to music. The scene is likely a Jewish celebration or gathering, such as a wedding or festive meal. The meme's intent is to humorously portray the man's enthusiastic, almost ecstatic, reaction to music, using the visual of a traditional religious figure in a moment of uninhibited joy. There is no evidence of toxicity, harmful content, or disparaging stereotypes. The meme relies on the contrast between the formal, traditional setting and the spontaneous, energetic movement, creating a comedic effect. The intent is purely lighthearted and satirical, not targeting any specific group with hate or abuse.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_88d2a42a"
      },
